                                        "sense_id": "637a682c-688d-32da-baff-e249b13dbbd6",
                                        "entry_id": "fdf3fd55-4468-3ee9-a2a3-11c1f2dbd741",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Especially sensitive, particularly to a stimulus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "669fcdcd-fa3e-3971-b715-bb71a9a6819b",
                                        "entry_id": "fdf3fd55-4468-3ee9-a2a3-11c1f2dbd741",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That, when subjected to a specific operation, will yield a specific result."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dff3af7-b652-4dce-9fac-5140e5bb3db0",
                                                "sense_id": "669fcdcd-fa3e-3971-b715-bb71a9a6819b",
                                                "text": "Rational numbers are susceptible of description as quotients of two integers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10d0b9dd-270f-4942-bc47-84237f5c8c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "669fcdcd-fa3e-3971-b715-bb71a9a6819b",
                                                "text": "A properly prepared surface is susceptible of an enduring paint job."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce84aac8-23c5-34b2-9524-a4adf805b7ec",
                                        "entry_id": "fdf3fd55-4468-3ee9-a2a3-11c1f2dbd741",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vulnerable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "810f2e64-1e7f-4246-99f3-bf26b8809bdd",
                                                "sense_id": "ce84aac8-23c5-34b2-9524-a4adf805b7ec",
                                                "text": "The visitors were being pinned back by the end of the first half. Yet Gordon Strachan's side played with great conviction and always had a chance of springing a surprise when their opponents were so susceptible at the back."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1423902-154c-32a2-b28a-5c7526a8f2c8",
                                        "entry_id": "fdf3fd55-4468-3ee9-a2a3-11c1f2dbd741",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Amenable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82e76019-250b-49fc-9744-474947b05cd0",
                                                "sense_id": "b1423902-154c-32a2-b28a-5c7526a8f2c8",
                                                "text": "In the next several chapters, we put the basic tools to work in different contexts with particular specification of return and transition equations designed to render the Bellman equation susceptible to further analysis and computation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "susceptible",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "099cc4e9-b141-3404-93eb-1121f2c2420c",
                                        "entry_id": "5782b078-e468-3f15-a248-25d061dcb8f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who is vulnerable to being infected by a certain disease"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e33220fc-abad-4ce3-8fdf-527b1338008d",
                                                "sense_id": "099cc4e9-b141-3404-93eb-1121f2c2420c",
                                                "text": "In either instance a decrease in the number of susceptibles, by making the spread of virus less easy, tends towards a stage at which the infection dies out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d9318878-e868-4ecb-b027-e573d66eb632",
                        "source_entry_id": "c73f3672-deb3-314a-91fa-f1e598b20149",
                        "source_sense_id": "9baeff33-5a48-37df-b069-91b0b08028d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "amative",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "amative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cfccf79-799d-305d-b310-636c7388891a",
                                        "entry_id": "fc68289b-7df4-35a8-9ea2-9f6602208608",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to love; amorous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e04f852-cd7c-4207-9929-e054d8c07967",
                                                "sense_id": "9cfccf79-799d-305d-b310-636c7388891a",
                                                "text": "1898, His amative enthusiasm, at which he is himself laughing, and his clever, imaginative, humorous ways, contrast strongly with the sincere tenderness and dignified quietness of the woman. : George Bernard Shaw, The Philanderer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92d55c49-db7a-4794-95a3-caa7729dc3f1",
                                                "sense_id": "9cfccf79-799d-305d-b310-636c7388891a",
                                                "text": "He was also confounded by its implication in Podson. Damme, the idea of that runt of a feller makin' up to a woman old enough to be his mother! Bradly banged pots about the stove, preparing the evening meal, to relieve himself of an outraged sense of propriety at Podson's amative presumption."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9e47b73-ebc2-4c2d-be4d-0386517da25a",
                                                "sense_id": "9cfccf79-799d-305d-b310-636c7388891a",
                                                "text": "His endearments were not amative or effete, but manly like Churchill's, and gave one a sense of being singled out, of having value."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
